{"id":"t06-143dab","status":"read","groups":[{"levels":[[{"surface":"أبو بكر بن أبي شيبة","kind":"narrator"},{"surface":"عمرو الناقد","kind":"narrator"}],[{"surface":"ابن عيينة","kind":"narrator"}]]},{"levels":[[{"surface":"قتيبة بن سعيد","kind":"narrator"}],[{"surface":"عبد العزيز","kind":"narrator"}]]},{"levels":[[{"surface":"أبو كريب","kind":"narrator"},{"surface":"إسحاق بن إبراهيم","kind":"narrator"}],[{"surface":"وكيع","kind":"narrator"}],[{"surface":"سفيان","kind":"narrator"}]]},{"levels":[[{"surface":"يحيى بن يحيى","kind":"narrator"}]],"variant":true}],"shared_tail":[[{"surface":"زيد بن أسلم","kind":"narrator"}],[{"surface":"عبد الرحمن بن وعلة","kind":"narrator"}],[{"surface":"ابن عباس","kind":"narrator"}]],"needs_ruling":false,"notes":["Three taḥwīl branches; the text writes «كلهم عن زيد بن أسلم» once after the last «ح», so Zayd, Abd al-Rahman and Ibn Abbas are the shared tail for all three.","«بمثله يعني حديث يحيى بن يحيى» names a different transmitter for the same saying: a variant group. The gloss «يعني ابن محمد» on «عبد العزيز» is left out."],"fixes":[]}
